{:edb/db-before-t 1671 :edb/db-after-t 1672 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534984 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:55:05.805Z" 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186064102 1071 "Given that $\\dfrac{6y - 1}{3} = ay + b$, what are the values of $a$ and $b$?" 13194139534984 17592186045417 false] [17592186064102 1071 "Given that $\\dfrac{6y − 1}{3} = ay + b,$  what are the values of $a$ and $b?$" 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186064102 1074 "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in the individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{6y - 1}{3} &= \\ \\dfrac{6y}{3} - \\dfrac 1 3 &= \\ \\dfrac{6}{3} \\cdot y - \\dfrac 1 3 \\\\ &= 2 \\cdot y - \\dfrac 1 3 \\\\ &= 2y - \\dfrac 1 3 &. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above in the form $ay+b$, we get\n\n$$\n(2)_(⏟)_(a)y + (-\\frac{1}{3})_(⏟)_(b)\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2$ and\n\n$$\nb=-\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$" 13194139534984 17592186045417 false] [17592186064102 1074 "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in the individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{6y − 1}{3} &= \\\n\t\t\\dfrac{6y}{3} - \\dfrac 1 3 &= \\\n\t\t\\dfrac{6}{3} \\cdot y - \\dfrac 1 3 &= \\\t\n\t\t2 \\cdot y - \\dfrac 1 3 &= \\\t\t\n\t\t2y - \\dfrac 1 3 &.\n\t}\n$$\n\nWriting the above in the form $ay+b,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{(2)}_{⏟}}_{a}y+{{(-\\frac{1}{3})}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2$ and $b=-\\dfrac{1}{3}.$" 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186064103 1071 "Given that $\\dfrac{1 - 2a + 16b}{4} = p + qa + rb$, what are the values of $p$, $q$, and $r$?" 13194139534984 17592186045417 false] [17592186064103 1071 "Given that $\\dfrac{1 − 2a + 16b}{4} = p + qa + rb,$ what are the values of $p,$ $q,$ and $r?$" 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186064103 1074 "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in the individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{1 - 2a + 16b}{4} &= \\ \\dfrac 1 4 - \\dfrac {2a} {4} + \\dfrac {16b}{4} &= \\ \\dfrac 1 4 - \\dfrac {2} {4} \\cdot a + \\dfrac {16}{4} \\cdot b &= \\ \\dfrac 1 4 - \\dfrac {1} {2} \\cdot a + 4 \\cdot b &= \\ \\dfrac 1 4 - \\dfrac {a} {2} + 4b &= \\ \\dfrac{1}{4} - \\dfrac{1}{2}a + 4b &. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above in the form $p+qa+rb$, we get\n\n$$\n(\\frac{1}{4})_(⏟)_(p) + (-\\frac{1}{2})_(⏟)_(q)a + (4)_(⏟)_(r)b\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\np=\\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$\n\n$$\nq=-\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nand $r=4$." 13194139534984 17592186045417 false] [17592186064103 1074 "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in the individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{1 − 2a + 16b}{4} &= \\\n\t\t\\dfrac 1 4 − \\dfrac {2a} {4} + \\dfrac {16b}{4} &= \\\n\t\t\\dfrac 1 4 − \\dfrac {2} {4} \\cdot a + \\dfrac {16}{4} \\cdot b &= \\\n\t\t\\dfrac 1 4 − \\dfrac {1} {2} \\cdot a + 4 \\cdot b &= \\\t\t\n\t\t\\dfrac 1 4 − \\dfrac {a} {2} + 4b &= \\\n                \\dfrac{1}{4} - \\dfrac{1}{2}a + 4b &.\n\t}\n$$\n\nWriting the above in the form $p+qa+rb,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{(\\frac{1}{4})}_{⏟}}_{p}+{{(-\\frac{1}{2})}_{⏟}}_{q}a+{{(4)}_{⏟}}_{r}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\dfrac{1}{4},$ $q=-\\dfrac{1}{2},$ and $r=4.$" 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186064257 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446899 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186064257 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446901 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186064258 1038 #edb/ref 17592186446900 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186064444 1050 420.0 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186065367 1064 "Fractions that contain multiple terms in the numerator and a single term in the denominator can be split into separate terms.\n\nFor example,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {x + 2} {3} &= \\ \\dfrac x 3 + \\dfrac 2 3 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {3a - 4b + 1} {5} &= \\ \\dfrac {3a} 5 - \\dfrac {4b} 5 + \\dfrac 1 5. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOften, we're able to simplify the fractions in the individual terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac {10x + 9} {2} &= \\ \\dfrac {10x} {2} + \\dfrac 9 2 &= \\ \\dfrac {10} {2} \\cdot x + \\dfrac 9 2 \\\\ &= 5 \\cdot x + \\dfrac 9 2 \\\\ &= 5x + \\dfrac 9 2 \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534984 17592186045417 false] [17592186065367 1064 "Fractions that contain multiple terms in the numerator and a single term in the denominator can be split into separate terms.\n\nFor example, \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {x + 2} {3} &= \\\n\t\t\\dfrac x 3 + \\dfrac 2 3\n\t}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {3a - 4b + 1} {5} &= \\\n\t\t\\dfrac {3a} 5 - \\dfrac {4b} 5 + \\dfrac 1 5.\n\t}\n$$\n\nOften, we're able to simplify the fractions in the individual terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {10x + 9} {2} &= \\\n\t\t\\dfrac {10x} {2} + \\dfrac 9 2 &= \\\n\t\t\\dfrac {10} {2} \\cdot x + \\dfrac 9 2 &= \\\t\n\t\t5 \\cdot x + \\dfrac 9 2 &= \\\n\t\t5x + \\dfrac 9 2 \n\t}\n$$" 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186233685 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446896 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186446875 1080 "2x-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186446875 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186446875 1083 #uuid "01a02ab5-3cde-53e5-8def-fa56bb2f44e2" 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186446876 1080 "3x+\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186446876 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186446876 1083 #uuid "41737690-1985-5531-8052-7be9b91b3f57" 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186446877 1080 "\\frac{a}{4}+\\frac{5b}{4}-\\frac{3c}{4}" 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186446877 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186446877 1083 #uuid "48a6505d-1142-59a6-8de5-35951e5ab5d3" 13194139534984 17592186045417 true] [17592186446878 1080 "2a+\\frac{5b}{4}+\\frac{3c}{2}" 13194139534984 17592186045417